    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class in the project, and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit (429 when 100+ owners already registered today), mirroring the existing `OwnerCityAtCapacity` rule pattern:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitReachedException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending `LocalDate`.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps the exception to **429 Too Many Requests** (`HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` constant and a `rejectDailyLimitReached()` check (counting existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the server's current date), wired into the `addOwner` reject chain right after the city-capacity check.\n\nThe check runs before persisting, counts existing owners created today by `registrationDate`, and throws once the count reaches 100 \u2014 so the 101st create in a day is rejected with 429.",
